From: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] gicv3: Mark gic_version unused when assertions are off

gicv3_driver_init() reads the GIC architecture revision into gic_version
purely to assert it is GICv3. This build sets ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=0, so
assert() expands to nothing and the variable is written but never read.
GCC 14 promoted that to an error by default, breaking do_compile:

  gicv3_main.c:60:22: error: variable 'gic_version' set but not used
  [-Werror=unused-but-set-variable=]

Tag it __unused, which is this tree's own idiom for a value needed only
by an assert -- it is defined in lib/stdlib/sys/cdefs.h, reachable here
via assert.h, and already used in 46 places. The read of GICD_PIDR2 is
kept so the assert still works when assertions are enabled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no upstream]

The codeaurora qoriq-components/atf branch this recipe pins was shut
down with the rest of source.codeaurora.org; upstream TF-A fixed the
same defect independently.

Signed-off-by: Luciano Dittgen <luciano.dittgen@ossystems.com.br>
---
 drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c b/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
--- a/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
+++ b/drivers/arm/gic/v3/gicv3_main.c
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ void gicv3_driver_init(const gicv3_driver_data_t *plat_driver_data)
  ******************************************************************************/
 void gicv3_driver_init(const gicv3_driver_data_t *plat_driver_data)
 {
-	unsigned int gic_version;
+	unsigned int gic_version __unused;
 
 	assert(plat_driver_data);
 	assert(plat_driver_data->gicd_base);
